  substitution here is triple-braced: a double brace turns the apostrophe in a
  copyright line into &#x27;, and a notice is not allowed to be approximately
  correct.

  Crates with a null `source` came from a path in this repository, so they are
  Sonduit's own and belong under the root LICENSE, not in a third-party file.

  The texts are iterated from `licenses` rather than from `overview`.
  `overview` holds one text per licence identifier, which sounds like what a
  deduplicated notice wants until you read the result: its MIT entry is
  whichever crate's copy was read first, so every MIT crate in the tree would
  ship under a single "Copyright (c) Microsoft Corporation" line. `licenses`
  is one entry per distinct text: identical boilerplate is merged and the
  copyright lines that differ survive, which is the whole of what MIT and the
  BSD licences require.
